LevitateOS License Information
===============================

This project contains multiple components with different licenses:


1. LEVITATEOS SOURCE CODE
-------------------------
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0 (dual-licensed)
Copyright (c) 2024-2026 LevitateOS Contributors

All LevitateOS source code is dual-licensed under MIT and Apache-2.0.
You may choose either license. See LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE.
Full texts of the other licenses named below (BSD-2-Clause, GPL-2.0,
GPL-3.0, LGPL-2.1) are in the LICENSES/ folder.

This includes:
  - Rust crates (distro/*, tools/*, testing/*, xtask)
  - TypeScript packages (docs/content, docs/website, tools/tui/*)

Contributions are accepted under the same dual license (inbound = outbound).


2. LEVITATEOS ISO - BUILT FROM FEDORA PACKAGES
----------------------------------------------
LevitateOS is an independent operating system. Its image is built from the
Fedora 45 RPM packages pinned in distro/builder/os-recipes/sources/ and from
LevitateOS's own programs, with a Linux kernel built from pinned kernel.org
source (section 4). The packages are third-party software, each under its own
license; Fedora's packages carry their license texts in /usr/share/licenses of
the installed system. Examples (the exact expressions are in SOURCES.txt):

  - systemd                : LGPL-2.1-or-later
  - GNU coreutils          : GPL-3.0-or-later
  - bash                   : GPL-3.0-or-later
  - util-linux             : GPL-2.0-or-later
  - NetworkManager         : GPL-2.0-or-later

The exact source package of every RPM, with its license, is listed in
SOURCES.txt, which is published with each release (section 7).


3. ACORNOS ISO - BUILT FROM ALPINE PACKAGES
-------------------------------------------
AcornOS is an independent operating system. Its image is built from the
Alpine Linux 3.24 APK packages pinned in distro/builder/os-recipes/sources/
and from LevitateOS's own programs, with a Linux kernel built from pinned
kernel.org source (section 4). The packages are third-party software, each
under its own license. Examples (the exact expressions are in SOURCES.txt):

  - musl                   : MIT
  - busybox                : GPL-2.0-only
  - OpenRC                 : BSD-2-Clause
  - eudev                  : GPL-2.0-or-later
  - bash                   : GPL-3.0-or-later
  - coreutils              : GPL-3.0-or-later

Alpine's packages carry the name of their license, not its text; the texts are
at https://levitateos.org/acorn/licenses. The origin (source package) of every
APK, with its license and the Alpine aports commit it was built from, is listed
in SOURCES.txt, which is published with each release (section 7).


4. LINUX KERNEL SOURCE AVAILABILITY
-----------------------------------
Both systems run a Linux kernel that LevitateOS builds from the vanilla
kernel.org source tarball, pinned by version and SHA-256 in
distro/builder/os-recipes/kernel/metadata.rhai (LevitateOS: the latest line,
AcornOS: a long-term-support line), with no patches. Only the configuration is
LevitateOS's: distro/variants/_shared/kconfig and distro/variants/*/kconfig,
which are MIT OR Apache-2.0 licensed.

  License: GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note
  Source : the tarball URL in SOURCES.txt (https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/)


5. RUST DEPENDENCIES
--------------------
LevitateOS's programs depend on external Rust crates under permissive
licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, Unicode-3.0, CC0-1.0,
Unlicense, MPL-2.0, Zlib, CDLA-Permissive-2.0), and no copyleft license
(GPL, AGPL, SSPL).

Verification: run `cargo deny check licenses` from the repository root.
Configuration: deny.toml


6. DISTRIBUTION OBLIGATIONS
---------------------------
If you distribute LevitateOS or AcornOS images, you must:

  a) Include this LICENSE file or equivalent notices
  b) Provide access to source code for GPL/LGPL components
  c) Preserve copyright notices

Source availability for GPL/LGPL compliance is described in section 7.


7. SOURCE CODE OF A RELEASE
---------------------------
Each release publishes SOURCES.txt as an asset of the release in
https://github.com/LevitateOS/releases. It lists, for every package and
component of the release, its name, version, license, source URL and hash. The
image carries the same notice and the written offer in
/usr/share/doc/levitate/LICENSES.txt.

For at least three years after the release, on request to the project's issue
tracker (https://github.com/LevitateOS/LevitateOS/issues) we provide the
complete corresponding source code of every GPL- and LGPL-licensed program in
the release on a medium customarily used for software interchange, for no more
than the cost of physically performing the distribution. The exact upstream
source packages and their hashes are listed in SOURCES.txt.

Upstream sources:

  Fedora packages:    https://src.fedoraproject.org
  Alpine packages:    https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports
  Linux kernel:       https://www.kernel.org


8. FULL LICENSE TEXTS
---------------------
LevitateOS code: LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE. The LICENSES/ directory:

  LICENSES/GPL-2.0.txt       Linux kernel, busybox, util-linux
  LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt       GNU coreutils, bash
  LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt      systemd
  LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt  OpenRC
